---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
import { rates, gbp, fractionalMonthly1Day, fractionalMonthly2Day } from '../data/rates';
import { testimonialsFor } from '../data/testimonials';
import TestimonialCarousel from '../components/TestimonialCarousel.astro';
import { faqsFor } from '../data/faqs';
import RelatedReading from '../components/RelatedReading.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import WhoFor from '../components/WhoFor.astro';
import { PRIMARY_PHRASE } from '../data/positioning';
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../data/links';


const testimonials = testimonialsFor('fractional');
const fractionalFaqs = faqsFor('fractional');

const serviceSchema = {
  '@type': 'Service',
  '@id': 'https://intentionaut.com/fractional/#service',
  name: 'Fractional & Interim Product Leadership',
  serviceType: 'Fractional product leadership',
  description:
    'Director-level product leadership for a defined period: one or two days a week, one month minimum then 30 days\' notice either side, with executive stakeholder access and accountability for delivery.',
  provider: { '@id': 'https://intentionaut.com/#person' },
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'City', name: 'London' },
    { '@type': 'Country', name: 'United Kingdom' },
    'Europe',
  ],
  offers: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    priceCurrency: 'GBP',
    price: rates.fractional,
    // unitText is not an Offer property; the units live on the price specs.
    priceSpecification: [
      { '@type': 'UnitPriceSpecification', price: fractionalMonthly1Day, priceCurrency: 'GBP', unitText: 'month (1 day a week)' },
      { '@type': 'UnitPriceSpecification', price: fractionalMonthly2Day, priceCurrency: 'GBP', unitText: 'month (2 days a week)' },
      { '@type': 'UnitPriceSpecification', price: rates.fractional, priceCurrency: 'GBP', unitText: 'day' },
    ],
    availability: 'https://schema.org/LimitedAvailability',
  },
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: fractionalFaqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.answer.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim() },
  })),
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${PRIMARY_PHRASE}, London | Saielle DaSilva`}
  description="Fractional CPO for AI products, from Saielle DaSilva. Her products have served over 100 million customers, at Amazon, Sainsbury's and Cazoo. Based in London."
  jsonLd={[serviceSchema, faqSchema]}
  ogImage="/og/fractional.png"
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Leadership &amp; advisory</p>
      <h1>Product leadership from someone whose products have served over 100 million customers.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        For teams building AI products who need Director-level product and
        design leadership, one or two days a week.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn-primary" href={BOOKING_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a free call <span class="sr-only">(opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      </div>
      <ul class="problem-lines">
        <li>A product that works and nobody likes, with no agreement on why.</li>
        <li>Designers with nobody senior leading them.</li>
        <li>AI features where nobody can yet say what good looks like.</li>
        <li>AI tools haven't changed the team's ways of working, or its maturity.</li>
      </ul>
      <WhoFor
        fit={[
          'Founders and CEOs who need Director-level product leadership now.',
          'Scale-ups whose product leader has left, or whose growth has outrun the team. <a href="/for-scale-ups/">Product leadership for scale-ups</a>.',
          'Teams with a product that works and no agreement on why it is not landing.',
          'Designers and product managers with nobody senior leading them.',
          'Companies shipping AI features without an agreed view of what good looks like.',
        ]}
        notFit={[
          'You are ready to hire a permanent head of product now. A search is the better route, and a fractional leader can help shape the role.',
          'You need one decision made or one plan reviewed, not ongoing leadership. 90 minutes of <a href="/office-hours/">office hours</a> covers that, and it can also be the first step into fractional work.',
          'You need something built rather than led. <a href="/forward-deployed/">Product building</a> embeds for four to twelve weeks and ends in a prototype or in software your team can run.',
        ]}
      />
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Sometimes you do not need a consultant. You need someone who will
        own the problem. Someone who shows up, makes the hard calls,
        leads the team and stays accountable for the outcome.
      </p>

      <h2>What does a fractional product leader do?</h2>
      <p>
        I become your senior product leader for a defined period. Typically
        one or two days a week, over three to six months. I have executive
        stakeholder access, I lead the team, I make strategic decisions and
        I am accountable for delivery.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is not advisory from the sidelines. It is leadership from
        inside the organisation, with the same authority and accountability
        as a permanent Director.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can check how that works. Each engagement agrees a small set of
        product KPIs at the start, and you review them together on a set
        rhythm. Saielle DaSilva works directly with your team's data, not a
        summary of it. She leads the team day to day and has access to your
        executive stakeholders.
      </p>

      <h2>What do you get?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Strategic decisions and product direction</li>
        <li>Team leadership and coaching</li>
        <li>Product operating model design and run</li>
        <li>Executive stakeholder management</li>
        <li>Delivery accountability and outcomes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How does it work?</h2>
      <p>
        A minimum commitment of one month, then 30 days' notice either side.
        Day rate {gbp(rates.fractional)}.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>One day a week, {gbp(fractionalMonthly1Day)} a month.</strong>
        Saielle DaSilva advises, challenges and guides. Your team leads the work.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Monthly strategy review with leadership</li>
        <li>Fortnightly coaching for your product lead</li>
        <li>Roadmap challenge before each planning cycle</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Two days a week, {gbp(fractionalMonthly2Day)} a month.</strong>
        Saielle DaSilva leads the work alongside your team, setting new ways of
        working and scaling them.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Owns the roadmap and the planning rhythm</li>
        <li>Weekly product reviews</li>
        <li>Hiring and coaching your PMs</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The engagement ends with a clear handover: a functioning team, an
        operating model that runs without me, and decisions that do not need
        relitigating.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sometimes what is missing is not direction but a working version of the
        idea, quickly. That is
        {' '}<a href="/forward-deployed/">product building</a>:
        three days a week in your environment, four weeks and up, building
        rather than leading.
      </p>

      <h2>Where has this been done before?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>As interim CPO at a direct-to-consumer grocery scaleup, monthly recurring revenue grew 450 per cent in 90 days.</li>
        <li>I led the product and design organisation at StepStone, with a 3.2x return on investment.</li>
        <li>At Sainsbury's I ran product for AI, data platforms and machine learning, and took production AI from a handful of experiments to dozens of generative AI systems.</li>
        <li>I was on the founding team at <a href="/case-studies/cazoo/">Cazoo</a>, through to a $7B IPO.</li>
      </ul>
      <TestimonialCarousel testimonials={testimonials} heading="What people say" />

      <h2>How do you start?</h2>
      <p>
        A free preliminary call. We check it is a fit. If it is, you get a
        written proposal: what we would do, when, and what it costs.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to test the fit before you commit? Start with a
        {' '}<a href="/office-hours/">office hours</a> session: {gbp(rates.strategySession)},
        90 minutes on your hardest product question. It works on its own, and
        it is also the first step into fractional work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Need more than one question answered? The
        {' '}<a href="/ai-product-audit/">AI product audit</a> ({gbp(rates.aiAudit)}, two days)
        and the <a href="/product-strategy-sprint/">product strategy sprint</a>
        {' '}({gbp(rates.strategySprint)}, four days) are fixed in scope and price.
        Either fee is credited against a fractional engagement that starts
        within 30 days.
      </p>
    </div>

    <RelatedReading href="/writing/impact-cant-bypass-politics/" title="Impact can't bypass politics" summary="Impact is decided by people before it is delivered by software." />

    <section class="contact-form-section" aria-label="Get in touch">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <h2>Let's talk.</h2>
        <p class="form-lede">
          If your team needs a senior product leader who will own the problem
          and stay until it is solved, let us talk.
        </p>
        <ContactForm source="fractional" selected="fractional" booking referral />
      </div>
    </section>

    <FaqList
      heading="FAQ: Fractional and interim CPO"
      items={fractionalFaqs}
      sub="What founders ask before bringing in a fractional CPO."
    />
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

